{
  "id": "3sum",
  "order": 29,
  "title": "3Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "pattern": "Sorting, two pointers",
  "statement": "Given an integer array `nums`, return all unique triplets `[a, b, c]` with `a + b + c = 0`. Each triplet must be sorted ascending, and the list of triplets must be sorted lexicographically.",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= nums.length <= 3000",
    "-10^5 <= nums[i] <= 10^5"
  ],
  "function": {
    "name": "threeSum",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "nums",
        "type": "int[]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int[][]"
  },
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2)",
    "space": "O(1) extra (sorting aside)"
  },
  "hints": [
    "Triple loops are O(n^3) and create duplicates. Would sorting help?",
    "Fix the first element, then the problem becomes Two Sum on the sorted remainder.",
    "Sort; for each i (skipping repeated values) run two pointers l, r; on a hit, record and skip duplicates of l."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1,
          2,
          -1,
          -4
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          -1,
          -1,
          2
        ],
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1
        ]
      ],
      "hidden": false,
      "explanation": "[[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]."
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          1,
          1
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [],
      "hidden": false,
      "explanation": "No triplet sums to 0."
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "hidden": false,
      "explanation": "One triplet."
    },
